      "content": "ok, that's more useful, thanks. so if bradykinin is building up because it's not being broken down, does that explain why some people get that dry cough? and is there any way the body tries to compensate for that extra bradykinin or the lower angiotensin II? like, does the system try to \"fight back\" in some way to restore the original balance?",
